Message-Id: <33df5e377a2a26a68c0d8040c82bc4c812b13d05.1794954871.git.336298264+yonto-app@users.noreply.github.com>
From: yonto-app <336298264+yonto-app@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:34:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bank: trust the plugins cache by a plugin's size alone

A Windows app package (MSIX) installs every file with the time it was
installed rather than its own, so the plugins.dat vlc-cache-gen writes
as the package is made never matched and libVLC opened every plugin on
each start. The cache is always written for the plugins it ships with,
by vlc-cache-gen beside them, so a plugin's size is enough to tell an
entry that is stale.
---
 src/modules/bank.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/modules/bank.c b/src/modules/bank.c
index 52037d5b59..e1e91d5dec 100644
--- a/src/modules/bank.c
+++ b/src/modules/bank.c
@@ -278,9 +278,10 @@ static int AllocatePluginFile (module_bank_t *bank, const char *abspath,
     {
         plugin = vlc_cache_lookup(&bank->cache, relpath);
 
+        /* By size alone: a Windows app package (MSIX) installs each file
+         * with the time it was installed, never the one the cache saw. */
         if (plugin != NULL
-         && (plugin->mtime != (int64_t)st->st_mtime
-          || plugin->size != (uint64_t)st->st_size))
+         && plugin->size != (uint64_t)st->st_size)
         {
             msg_Err(bank->obj, "stale plugins cache: modified %s",
                     plugin->abspath);
-- 
2.30.2

